  "text_sanskrit": "ये त्वेतदभ्यसूयन्तो नानुतिष्ठन्ति मे मतम् । सर्वज्ञानविमूढांस्तान्विद्धि नष्टानचेतसः ॥ ३-३२ ॥",
  "itrans": "ye tvetadabhyasUyanto nAnutiShThanti me matam . sarvaj~nAnavimUDhA.nstAnviddhi naShTAnachetasaH .. 3-32 ..",
  "translation": "But those who find fault with this teaching of Mine and neglect it, know those to be devoid of discrimination, entirely deluded as to all knowledge and (altogether) lost. (32)\nV. Find fault with: by saying or thinking that, Sri. Krishna is simply putting them to difficulties and imposing impossible duties upon them.\nBy means of actions: i.e., Nivritti Karma and the knowledge and wisdom resulting from their practice. They too: implies that there can be no possible question about the release of those who have attained the direct perception of the Lord. Devoid of discrimination: i.e., having perverse notions of all things to be known, Lost: doomed to sufferings in hell. (31, 32.) \nA. If it is true that the adoption of the teaching gives Moksha and its neglect brings destruction, why is it then that the world does not carefully follow the course? Here the Lord says:",
